The paper investigates periodic variations in the cosmic ray flux and spectral index measured by Antarctic neutron monitors, and shows that the spectral index variations tracked by the leader fraction parameter are strongly correlated with the solar magnetic sector structure, indicating particle drifts as a likely driver, while flux variations show additional influence from solar wind speed variations.
