[QA 0] The paper presents a comprehensive analysis demonstrating that sub-banded search techniques significantly enhance the detection of fast radio bursts, leading to the discovery of eighteen new bursts in the High Time Resolution Universe survey, nearly tripling the previous count. | The key contribution of this paper is the identification of 18 new fast radio bursts (FRBs) by applying a sub-banded search technique to reprocess data from the high-latitude portion of the High Time Resolution Universe (HTRU) South survey, nearly tripling the previous number of FRB detections from this survey.
[QA 1] This paper investigates the effects of porosity on the spectro-photometric properties of Phobos regolith simulants, revealing that high porosity can potentially explain the origin of the Phobos blue unit, while also observing modifications in emissivity and phase reddening that provide insights into surface roughness and scattering behavior. | The key contribution of this paper is that it investigated the effects of porosity on the spectro-photometric properties of Phobos regolith simulants, providing insights relevant for interpreting future observations of Phobos and Deimos by the MMX mission.
