[QA 3] The paper presents a compact, modular, and cost-effective motherboard controller designed for controlling twelve stepper motors in quadruped robots, validated through detailed power distribution network analysis and successful hardware testing, offering a scalable solution for bio-inspired robotic applications. | The key contribution of this paper is the design, analysis, fabrication and validation of a modular printed circuit board (PCB) hardware system to control twelve stepper motors for a quadruped robot.
[QA 4] The paper determines the exact Turán number for complete bipartite graphs with bounded matching number when the number of vertices and the parameters are sufficiently large, providing new insights into extremal graph theory for specific graph families. | The key contribution of this paper is determining the exact value of the Turán number ex(n, {K_l,t, M_s+1}) for complete bipartite graphs K_l,t with bounded matching number s+1, when s is sufficiently large with respect to l, or when t is sufficiently large with respect to s-l, for all 3 ≤ l ≤ t.
