[QA 3] The paper demonstrates that certain inhomogeneities, including those with corners or cusps, can support non-scattering frequencies under specific material conditions, challenging the assumption that geometric singularities always lead to scattering. | Here is a one sentence summary of the key contribution of the paper "Examples of non-scattering inhomogeneities":

